{"author":{"id":"b409816c5cd5ab140d1d52eb33aace35de44952bb794b19806fd57f6ecb1ace9"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1795430430,"nonce":"7c2nnNIGunnkYXU+1mmR7Dv0Qlc=","title":"Python: x in s on a set tests False for an unhashable x instead of raising TypeError","message":"At cb59570e, `[1] in {1, 2, 3}` and `[1] in {\"a\", \"b\"}` print False; CPython raises TypeError: cannot use 'list' as a set element (unhashable type: 'list'). A set of eight values or fewer is scanned without hashing, so the probe never reaches a hash. Split from 486ab62, whose KeyError message part is fixed. Dict lookups with an unhashable key should be checked in the same pass: d[[1]] and [1] in d.","files":null}]}